task_scratch=$(cat ~/.robob/board-artifacts/offbox-tmp-space/scratch-path.txt)
cat > "$task_scratch/report.py" <<'PY'
import json,pathlib,datetime
root=pathlib.Path.home()/'.robob/board-artifacts/offbox-tmp-space'
fleet=json.loads((root/'fleet.json').read_text());ledger=json.loads((root/'server-ledger.json').read_text());proof=json.loads((root/'attribution.json').read_text());g=1024**3
fmt=lambda n:f'{n/g:.3f} GiB'
iso=lambda t:datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t,datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds') if t else '—'
lines=['# Offbox #129: read-only tmp-space investigation','',f"Measured {fleet['at']} (UTC). Read-only; no files deleted, no box resumed/stopped, no profile or service changes. Only owner ardud boxes inspected. Proc holder results are point-in-time observations, not deletion authorization.",'','## Historical snapshot (cite, do not remeasure)','',"Card #129 evaluator snapshot ~01:08Z: 20 running boxes; bx_0jngiwmr and bx_vg810ggr each had tmpfs 8 GiB / 0 available, inodes only 1% used. bx_0jngiwmr held /tmp/tmp.4J4nhqYAvx ~7.6 GiB, owner user, mtime 00:56:58Z, no live holder. bx_vg810ggr held /tmp/tmp.jZIKTqEpfW ~7.8 GiB. Root ZFS had ample free space. bx_j7v4bnal was 19%; other boxes ≤5%. bx_61vytpaz, bx_asqfd287 and bx_uk4ext8o still used ZFS /tmp. This report preserves that evidence; it does not replace it with later readings.",'','## Current running home fleet','',"Inventory changed between the earlier offbox list and this probe: 15 running Incus boxes, including newly started bx_b5j336sn. bx_0jngiwmr was already archived at 01:24:13Z and was not resumed. Its tmpfs contents therefore no longer exist; rootfs logs were read with incus file pull without booting it. All 15 filesystem probes succeeded. findmnt uses -T so pre-rollout ZFS /tmp resolves to its containing / mount.",'','| Box | Started UTC | Running age | /tmp fs | Size | Used | Free | /var/tmp free | $HOME free |','|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
summary=lines[-2:]
for r in fleet['boxes']:
 fs=r['filesystems']['/tmp'];used=fs['size_bytes']-fs['free_bytes'];r['summary']={'fstype':r['findmnt']['out'].split()[0],'size_bytes':fs['size_bytes'],'used_bytes':used,'free_bytes':fs['free_bytes']}
 row=f"| {r['box_id']} | {r['started_at'][11:19]} | {float(r['uptime'])/3600:.2f} h | {r['summary']['fstype']} | {fmt(fs['size_bytes'])} | {fmt(used)} | {fmt(fs['free_bytes'])} | {fmt(r['filesystems']['/var/tmp']['free_bytes'])} | {fmt(r['filesystems']['/home/user']['free_bytes'])} |"
 lines.append(row);summary.append(row)
lines += ['','## Top entries and process holders','',"du -x -B1 --max-depth=1 /tmp plus allocated bytes for top-level files; largest 10 entries, including hidden entries. UID/owner and top-entry mtime from lstat. Live holders: cwd/root symlinks, open fds and file-backed mmap paths in /proc, excluding the probe itself. Concurrent process/file creation can race the snapshot; no deletion follows from this read-only scan."]
for r in fleet['boxes']:
 lines += ['',f"### {r['box_id']}",'',f"findmnt: `{r['findmnt']['out']}`",'', '```text',r['df']['out'],'```','',f"Top-level entry count: {r['entries']}; du warnings: {r['du_error'] or 'none'}.",'','| Entry | Allocated | Owner (uid) | Mtime UTC | Live holders |','|---|---:|---|---|---|']
 for path,e in r['top10'].items():
  holders='; '.join(f"pid {h['pid']} ({','.join(h['via'])})" for h in e['holders']) or 'none observed'
  lines.append(f"| {path} | {fmt(e['bytes'])} | {e.get('owner')} ({e.get('uid')}) | {e.get('mtime')} | {holders} |")
lines += ['','## Leaking runs: server ledger and retained receipts','', '| Box / path | Run / command | Started UTC | Ended UTC | End state |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
for r in proof['runs']:
 path='tmp.jZIKTqEpfW' if r['box_id']=='bx_vg810ggr' else 'tmp.4J4nhqYAvx'
 lines.append(f"| {r['box_id']}:/tmp/{path} | {r['run_id']} / {r['pid']} / {r['command_id']} | {iso(r['started_at'])} | {iso(r['ended_at'])} | {r['status']}, exit {r['exit_code']}, signal {r['signal']}, attempt {r['attempt']} |")
 lines += ['',f"Retained inner log `{r['inner_log_path']}`:",'','```text',r['inner_log'].strip(),'```']
lines += ['',"Both are `bash scripts/sqlite-disk-wait/full.sh base-2|base-3 base baseline` in /home/user/w/sqlite-disk-wait-base-4d64d9. Neither was killed nor timed out: status exited, exit_code=1, signal=NULL, attempt=1 in ledger AND result receipt. The earlier writer probe run-1114-043233-9a5a (pid 1443) ended 00:41:34Z with SIGTERM/143, but is not the source of these two directories.",'',"At 8d067e0fd8, scripts/sqlite-disk-wait/userspace-run.sh uses `export IODELAY_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d)\"`, then `cp -a --reflink=auto \"$IODELAY_TEMPLATE_DIR/.\" \"$IODELAY_DIR/\"` under `set -euo pipefail`, without an EXIT cleanup trap. The copy fails with ENOSPC and exits before the workload launches. Thus these were partial template copies, not completed 4,404-thread benchmark homes. tmpfs cannot reflink the ZFS source, so the copy consumes RAM-backed bytes. The Robob board already owns the harness leak fix; #129 only records attribution.",'','## #128 timing and confidence','',"Producer run-1114-043508-8c88 exited at 00:57:02.017Z with three explicit ENOSPC copy errors naming /tmp/tmp.4J4nhqYAvx. Evaluator mtime was 00:56:58Z. Victim run-1114-045753-9655 (pid 1445, cmd_8016af9e18675368) started 00:58:45.024Z; Vitest started 00:58:54Z and ran 26.94 seconds. Server-retained stderr reports ENOENT opening /tmp/bywqrbApTLQ7o7Poj1GHX/ssr/4a285db7953304824777650c487cd326317a8b90. It exited 1 at 00:59:40.014Z. Later evaluator df at ~01:08Z shows 0 free; the next venv run 050126 failed with ENOSPC. Nobody had manually cleaned the box.",'',"Conclusion: /tmp exhaustion immediately predates #128 and explains the SSR symptom strongly; there is no evidence of a deleter in this investigation. Exact 0-byte availability during 00:58:54–00:59:21Z is NOT independently measured: neither run metadata nor host_samples captured per-box tmp free bytes then. Do not claim a timestamped df exists or rule out other causes solely from ENOENT. #128 should continue its private TMPDIR/own teardown scope, with this run treated as infra-contaminated evidence rather than proof of deletion.",'','## Host memory and cap recommendation','',f"Host MemTotal={ledger['host_meminfo']['MemTotal']} = 92.00 GiB usable (96 GB installed); current MemAvailable={ledger['host_meminfo']['MemAvailable']} = {int(ledger['host_meminfo']['MemAvailable'].split()[0])/1024**2:.2f} GiB; swap=0. 306 host_samples from 00:20–01:15Z show 18–23 live boxes, at most 20 running commands, and minimum MemAvailable 29.77 GiB. Current snapshot: 15 boxes. Both full boxes were 24/48 GiB size classes, not 8 GiB small boxes.",'',"Keep the 8 GiB ceiling for now. It is demand-backed, not reserved; 15×8 GiB already exceeds host RAM if all boxes fill it. Raising it would let unbounded leaked copies consume more RAM and still fill any finite cap. Free-space gating + cleanup is the targeted fix; large intentional scratch should use a private $HOME directory (with the known ZFS Unicode limitation). Retain executable tmpfs for Unicode-safe /tmp. Any cap/profile change remains #67's scope; none applied.",'','## Boat standby','',"OFFBOX_BACKEND=boat offbox list --all: 237 boxes, all stopped (boat-list.txt). No Boat box was started or resumed for this read-only step, so a live Boat findmnt/df is unavailable. The 8 GiB tmpfs cap comes from home-only server/install-host.sh tmp_profile(), not server/boatd.py or common client templates. Boat is an external backend; source inspection cannot certify its guest mount type/cap. Shared pre/post run checks should cover it when implemented; a live standby observation remains for the next already-running Boat lease.",'','## Implementation handoff / limits','',"No implementation edits, commits, install or deploy in this step. Shared root checkout is on fix/631-identity-indexes with unrelated work; implementation needs its own worktree at current origin/main. Current source and host_samples do not have per-box tmp-space fields; #123 host load work remains separate. #128 owns private TMPDIR/teardown; #129 owns gate/classification/reaper. Deletion ask q1 is still open; bx_vg810ggr remains full. No cleanup has been attempted.",'',"Artifacts: fleet.json (per-box raw mount/df/top10/proc metadata); server-ledger.json (relevant command metadata + host samples); attribution.json (exact producing commands, receipts, inner ENOSPC logs, victim stderr); boat-list.txt; this fleet.md. Scratch scripts reside in the private mktemp directory referenced by scratch-path.txt."]
(root/'fleet.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');(root/'fleet-summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(summary)+'\n');(root/'fleet.json').write_text(json.dumps(fleet,indent=2)+'\n')
for r in proof['runs']:(root/(r['run_id']+'-inner.log')).write_text(r['inner_log'])
(root/'run-1114-045753-9655-stderr.log').write_text(proof['victim']['stderr'])
print('Wrote',root/'fleet.md','bytes',(root/'fleet.md').stat().st_size,'boxes',len(fleet['boxes']))
PY
python3 -I "$task_scratch/report.py"